## FRESH MONEY TEST
**Fresh money allocation: 12%**

The gap between 12% (fresh money) and 18% (recommended maximum) reflects two factors: (1) the company has no multi-quarter gross margin track record yet — this is the first positive gross margin quarter, and Sandra Wallach explicitly cautioned that "we are still too small to definitively state that we have reached a steady state"; (2) the ATM equity issuance program ($9.8M in Q2 alone, 3.2M shares) creates ongoing dilution that a fresh buyer absorbs fully, while an existing holder has already absorbed prior dilution. The gap is not inertia — the thesis is genuinely strengthening — but a fresh buyer should size conservatively until at least two consecutive quarters of positive gross margin are confirmed and the South Korea ramp demonstrates commercial-scale output.

